# name: test_error_message[identity_comparison.py]
  '''
  identity_comparison.py:4:8: error: `is` doesn't make sense once compiled to C++
  
    4 |     if a is b:
      |        ^^^^^^
  
    help: every value is independent once compiled, so there's no separate notion of identity - use == if you meant to compare values:
            a == b
  
  '''
