# name: test_error_message[object_element.py]
  '''
  object_element.py:2:15: error: Type of expression is inferred as `list[object]` which contains `object`. This cannot be translated to C++.
  
    2 |     print(any([False, True]))
      |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  
    help: Everything must have strictly one type only. There may be multiple different types being assigned to the field with type `object`. You can give this expression a type annotation to help you catch the error.
  
  '''
