# name: test_error_message[stale_loop_variable.py]
  '''
  stale_loop_variable.py:4:11: error: `i` is read after the `for` loop that bound it has ended
  
    4 |     print(i)
      |           ^
  
    help: C++'s for loop leaves its counter one past the last value used, unlike Python, so this would read a different value here. Assign it to another variable inside the loop body instead:
            for i in range(5):
                i_last = i
            print(i_last)
  
  '''
